WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:08.541
Hey youtubers it’s charlie and this week
agents of shield introduced a new major comic

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:09.740
book character and stan lee made his illustrious
cameo.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.530
It’s not a two parter, but the next episode
is a direct continuation.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.610
which is great because I love serialized shows.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:18.730
Since a lot of you in the UK won’t get to
see this for a while careful for potential

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:19.730
spoilers.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:20.830
Marvel already announced who it is, but in
case you still don’t know I’ll save it

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.199
for the end of the video.

00:00:22.199 --> 00:00:24.649
Let’s start with our top 5 moments and then
I’ll do my review.

00:00:24.649 --> 00:00:26.619
Number 5 - May’s wheels up in 5.

00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:29.141
I’m talking about the whole reverse storyline
aspect of the episode.

00:00:29.141 --> 00:00:33.440
I thought it added a really nice touch to
the story and it was so much fun watching

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.000
what happened to May after she got knocked
off the train.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.399
Notice that the May story was bookeneded by
Ward’s sex talk with Coulson.

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:44.440
I got the sense that they wanted us to visually
connect May’s intensity with her relationship

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:45.440
with ward.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.510
Especially that torture scene.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:51.340
It’s a nice reversal to see a female character
be so aggressive.

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:53.609
But I’ve always been a huge fan of ming
na.

00:00:53.609 --> 00:00:56.700
It’s great to see her get to have so much
fun.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:00.219
She has all the best action scenes on the
show.

00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:02.469
Number 4 - stan lee cameo.

00:01:02.469 --> 00:01:06.020
In true comic book fashion, stan lee serves
as the moral message of the episode.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:10.690
His comment to coulson, you’ve made mistakes,
but you can do better is really a generic

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:13.340
theme for all the characters and the audience.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:21.160
Particularly mike peterson’s character.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:23.550
Number 3 - Strangers on a train.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.060
Coulson and simmons epic blowout was a lot
of fun to watch.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:30.550
I liked how they paid off fitz’s earlier
jokes about how she’s the queen of homework.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:33.880
The look on coulson’s face when she said
prostitutes was priceless.

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.780
I can see the hashtags now.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:37.780
#prostituteface

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:40.290
Number 2 - Skye and simmons are pretty dead.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.050
Not one but two almost deaths.

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:47.890
There were maybe three game changing events
in this episode and sky and simmons were two

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:48.890
of those.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:52.610
Simmons is just frozen as a result of the
night night gun gas, but skye is bleeding

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:53.610
out.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:57.210
I actually expected her to manifest a power
in that post credits teaser, so it looks like

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:59.350
she doesn’t have any resurgence abilities.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:05.200
My earlier theory was that she was a technopath.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.479
Number 1 - Mike Peterson becomes deathlok.

00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:11.269
I like the way they explain how he’s deathlok.

00:02:11.269 --> 00:02:13.040
Just by using the cybernetik leg.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:17.140
In the comic books, the character is more
machine than man darth vader style.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:20.370
But they opted to make J august richards look
more realistic.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:23.269
I’m calling that the tyrion lannister move.

00:02:23.269 --> 00:02:27.330
When a show dramatically reduces injuries
or alterations to a character that would make

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:30.609
them have to wear crazy prosthetics and special
effects.

00:02:30.609 --> 00:02:34.330
They did incorporate some of the story from
the Michael Collins deathlok in the comic

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.330
books.

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:39.290
He had his brain put in a cybernetic body
and was being controlled by the machine parts.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:42.560
Eventually he gained control of his body and
became a SHIELD agent.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:46.480
Honorable mention goes to coulson for laying
the smack down on ward during their sex talk.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.049
He threatened to put him on emil blonsky duty
in alaska.

00:02:48.049 --> 00:02:50.519
Remember he was the hulk villain called the
abomination.

00:02:50.519 --> 00:02:54.340
The last person to play that character was
Tim Roth in the incredible hulk.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.629
Let me know what your favorite moment was
and whether or not you think Skye’s power

00:02:56.629 --> 00:02:59.110
will manifest in the next episode.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.470
Personally seeing Mike become deathlok was
the high point of the episode.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.079
That or couslon prostitute face.

00:03:04.079 --> 00:03:06.659
Overall this was one of the strongest episodes
this season.

00:03:06.659 --> 00:03:10.290
I loved the narrative structure and the way
they told a lot of the story in reverse.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:14.910
And they were able to go from laugh out loud
funny on the train to almost killing the two

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:17.290
most loveable harmless female characters.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:21.829
It’s like Joss Whedon hurting willow on
buffy, she seems so harmless so it twists

00:03:21.829 --> 00:03:24.819
you up to watch them almost die.

00:03:24.819 --> 00:03:27.590
Agents of SHIELD isn’t a joss whedon show,
but if you’re ever watching something joss

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:29.909
whedon did and you really start to love a
character.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:33.469
Watch out, because they’re the one that’s
going to get hurt.

00:03:33.469 --> 00:03:36.989
You could also call that pulling a George
RR Martin.

00:03:36.989 --> 00:03:39.180
Stan Lee’s cameo felt appropriate.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:43.330
He kind of seems like he’s been play acting
hugh hefner in all of his recent movie cameos,

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:45.920
but the moral message he delivered was a comic
book trope that he started.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:46.920
At least in the style it was done during the
episode.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:47.920
Like at the end of old GI Joe cartoons.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.780
One of my favorite things about the episode
is how mike peterson’s arc just became one

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:52.430
of the most important things on the show.

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:54.489
He’ll be critical to them defeating the
clarivoyant.

00:03:54.489 --> 00:03:57.340
But he started out as this throwaway extremis
cameo.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:01.419
So I’m expecting a similar thing to happen
to Skye, she’s still in the middle of that

00:04:01.419 --> 00:04:05.519
moment of horror that peterson had when he
woke up burned missing limbs.

00:04:05.519 --> 00:04:09.390
So expect Skye’s character to undergo a
fundamental change once she recovers.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:13.180
I’m hoping that means that she finds out
what her powers are and starts using them.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:17.049
It’s like the show just told us, the only
way to survive is to evolve, sometimes that

00:04:17.049 --> 00:04:20.650
means becoming a cyborg and sometimes it means
manifesting special powers.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:23.070
I love science fiction so much.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.220
Big announcement.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:27.770
SHIELD is back until March 4th because of
the olympics.

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:30.440
When they do come back Bill paxton is guest
starring as another big shield agent.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:31.440
John Garret.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:32.440
In the comics he was a cyborg too.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:35.170
Think of his character as being like a hardcore
version of his hicks character from aliens.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.510
with less wisecracking.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.560
They just made some major casting announcements
for the new flash tv show.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.590
I’m going to be doing a special video for
that Thursday.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:46.500
So subscribe to get it.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.070
Right now click here for last week’s agents
of shield and click here to for my latest

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:51.070
arrow video.

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:52.680
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.260
High Fives!

